## the bundled cartopy coastline: EXEMPT from LFS, deliberately
# `data/cartopy/**` holds the 1.1 MB Natural Earth coastline every map figure needs (see data/cartopy/README.md).
# It is committed as ORDINARY blobs because making it an LFS object forces `git lfs install`, whose
# `filter.lfs.required = true` makes EVERY git command in the repo exit 128 when the binary is absent -- measured, not
# feared: `git status` fails, and the `git diff HEAD` that lazy.code_state_hash runs fails too, silently degrading the
# cache key to a hash of src/ alone. A hard runtime dependency on every machine is not worth 1.1 MB.
# ⚠️ This exemption is LOAD-BEARING. `*.shp filter=lfs` above still applies everywhere else, so removing these two
# lines lets the next commit by anyone with git-lfs installed convert the shapefile into a pointer -- after which
# cartopy dies with `KeyError: 828781878` inside shapefile.py, which reads as corrupt data rather than a missing tool.
# Scoped to `shapefiles/` rather than `data/cartopy/**` on purpose: `-diff` disables TEXTUAL diff too, and the wider
# pattern turned data/cartopy/README.md into an undiffable binary blob.
data/cartopy/shapefiles/** -filter -diff -merge
